overted issues.**\nL33@P0: 6. All counsel have prepared a list of stipulated facts and made a good faith effort to stipulate to as many documents,\nL34@P0: waiver of foundational requirements, etc., as reasonably possible.**\nL35@P0: 7. Each party agrees that once the trial commences, witnesses shall be available to utilize to the fullest extent possible\nL36@P0: every trial day.\nL37@P0: 8. Parties have agreed on a division of jury fees (if applicable) and reporter fees, which are due each day before trial\nL38@P0: commences.\nL39@P0:  , Attorney for Plf/Def/X-Compl/X-Def (SIGNATURE OF ATTORNEY) (NAME OF PARTY) (DATE)\nL40@P0:  , Attorney for Plf/Def/X-Compl/X-Def (SIGNATURE OF ATTORNEY) (NAME OF PARTY) (DATE)\nL41@P0:  , Attorney for Plf/Def/X-Compl/X-Def (SIGNATURE OF ATTORNEY) (NAME OF PARTY) (DATE)\nL42@P0:  , Attorney for Plf/Def/X-Compl/X-Def (SIGNATURE OF ATTORNEY) (NAME OF PARTY) (DATE)\nL43@P0: **Please attach to this Statement of Compliance: Joint Statement of Case, Joint Witness List, Stipulated Facts, Requested\nL44@P0: Voir Dire Questions and List of Controverted Issues.\n--------------------------------------------------------------------------------\nMicrosoft Word - FINAL 2015 Stipulation and Appointment of Official Reporter Pro Tempore (Rev 012215) (https://www.occourts.org/system/files/l0860.pdf)\nciteturn1464view1 [wordlim: 200] Crawled: last week; Content type: application/pdf; Number of pages: 2; Source: click({\"ref_id\":\"turn1411view1\",\"id\":385}); Total lines: 87\nL0@P0: Approved for Mandatory Use\nL1@P0: OCSC Form # L-0860 STIPULATION AND APPOINTMENT OF COURT REPORTER PRO TEMPORE Cal. Rules of Court, rule 2.956;\nL2@P0: Rev 1-22-15 Gov. Code §§ 68086\nL3@P0: Page 1 of 2\nL4@P0: ATTORNEY OR PARTY WITHOUT ATTORNEY (Name & Address):\nL5@P0: Telephone No.: Fax No. (Optional):\nL6@P0: E-Mail Address (Optional):\nL7@P0: ATTORNEY FOR (Name): Bar No:\nL8@P0: FOR COURT USE ONLY\nL9@P0: \nL10@P0: SUPERIOR COURT OF CALIFORNIA, COUNTY OF ORANGE\n